\description{
A unified UniFrac distance that balances the weight of abundant and rare lineages.
}
\details{
The Generalized UniFrac distance is defined as:
\deqn{\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n} L_i(P_i + Q_i)^{\alpha}\left|\frac{P_i - Q_i}{P_i + Q_i}\right|}{\sum_{i=1}^{n} L_i(P_i + Q_i)^{\alpha}}}

Where:
\itemize{
\item \eqn{n} : The number of branches in the tree.
\item \eqn{L_i} : The length of the \eqn{i}-th branch.
\item \eqn{P_i}, \eqn{Q_i} : The proportion of the community descending from branch \eqn{i} in sample P and Q.
\item \eqn{\alpha} : A scalable weighting factor.
}

\strong{Parameter: alpha}

The \code{alpha} parameter controls the weight given to abundant lineages. \eqn{\alpha = 1} corresponds to Weighted UniFrac, while \eqn{\alpha = 0} corresponds to Unweighted UniFrac.
}
